INFOS:
1. BASIC CORE SCORING
Matches are typically played to 11 points, win by 2. Points can only be scored by the serving team. In doubles, both partners have the opportunity to serve before the ball is turned over to the opposition.
2. SERVICE PROTOCOL
The serve must be hit with an underhand motion (paddle contact below the waist). The ball must travel diagonally across the net and clear the non-volley zone (the Kitchen) to be considered a legal serve.
3. TWO-BOUNCE RULE
Following the serve, each side must allow the ball to bounce once before playing it. Once the ball has bounced once on each side (the "double bounce"), players may choose to either volley the ball or play it off a bounce.
4. KITCHEN RULE
The 7-foot area adjacent to the net is the Non-Volley Zone. Players are prohibited from volleying the ball while standing within this zone. You may only enter the "Kitchen" if the ball bounces within it first.
5. COMPLETION OF A RALLY
A rally concludes when a player hits the ball out of bounds, fails to clear the net, or commits a "fault" (such as a Non-Volley Zone violation).



END TAGLINE: Reserve Your Game. Elevate Your Play.



